BLOCK FB FB_PusherControl
ROOTID 0
NUMBER 3
LANGUAGE LAD
TITLE "Pusher Control"
COMMENT "Pusher ram sequencing (C-118-C-125). Step legend (C-120): 0=Idle (no motion; home is the HomeLimit switch, not implied by the step - after a jog release the ram may legitimately rest off home, REQ-039) - 10=DriveToEndTravel (forward stroke in progress) - 20=Hold (paused at full travel, brief settle before retracting) - 30=Retract (returning to home; also the recovery/abort target from any bad state). Mode legend: 0=Off (finish a retract already in progress, then park; no new cycle starts) - 1=Auto (hopper-high-level starts a cycle) - 2=Manual (operator button/jog starts a cycle). Motion policy (owner rulings 2026-07-16): an idle off-home ram reparks ONLY on the plant pre-start ParkCmd or on a live cycle request - never on jog release or bare mode changes - and every motion start from rest (repark, cycle launch, jog) is preceded by the JogWarningTime sounder warning (NEW-4: no unwarned pusher motion). CycleInhibit (any live plant stop reason) blocks cycle launches and aborts an in-flight cycle to park, but deliberately leaves hand-jog available - only the mode-0 force (stop button/unhealthy) blocks jogging (owner amendment 2026-07-16, REQ-040). Fitted=FALSE (REQ-042/043/044) kills every demand, the pack output, both supervision timers, and every fault latch at the source, so a disabled pusher does nothing and raises nothing."

INTERFACE
  INPUT
  OUTPUT
  STATIC
    IO : "UDT_PusherIO" RETAIN SETPOINT COMMENT "Caller-visible interface (C-115) - FC_ControlMain writes Mode/HopperHighLevel/limits/tunables in, reads Extend/Retract/RunPowerPack/fault bits out. See the block header for the Step/Mode value legend."
      Step : Int
      Fitted : Bool
      Enable : Bool
      Mode : Int
      HopperHighLevel : Bool
      ManualCycleCmd : Bool
      ParkCmd : Bool
      CycleInhibit : Bool
      JogExtendCmd : Bool
      JogRetractCmd : Bool
      HomeLimit : Bool
      FullTravelLimit : Bool
      HighPressure : Bool
      PowerPackRunningFB : Bool
      FaultReset : Bool
      EndTravelTimeout : Real
      ParkedTimeout : Real
      EndTravelHoldTime : Real
      PumpRunOnTime : Real
      JogWarningTime : Real
      PressureTripConfirmTime : Real
      PressureClearResumeDelay : Real
      PressureTripCountThreshold : Int
      Cycling : Bool
      Blocked : Bool
      EndTravelTimeoutFault : Bool
      ParkedTimeoutFault : Bool
      BothSwitchesFault : Bool
      RunPowerPack : Bool
      Extend : Bool
      Retract : Bool
      JogPreStartSounder : Bool
    CycleRequest : Bool COMMENT "Named once, read everywhere (C-601): the live cycle trigger - Auto on hopper high or Manual on the HMI button - gated by Enable (Fitted AND not Off) and NOT Blocked. Read by the warning armer, the launch and repark transitions, and the trip-count reset. Blocked is written later in the scan, so this reads it one scan behind - immaterial: Blocked can only latch mid-stroke (Step 10) where no Step 0 request can act, and a reset-clear merely delays a relaunch by one scan."
    JogDemand : Bool COMMENT "A live jog request: either jog button held, idle, Manual mode, pusher fitted. Arms the pre-motion warning, suppresses the repark (jogging is never fought by an auto-retract), and - per direction, warning done - drives the demands. Reads Step from before this scan's transitions; the demand rungs re-check Step fresh."
    ReparkRequest : Bool COMMENT "A repark to home is wanted: the sequencer's pre-start ParkCmd (REQ-045) or a live CycleRequest, while idle off home and not jogging. One of the only two motion sources out of Step 0 (owner ruling 2026-07-16); fires the 0-to-30 transition once the pre-motion warning has sounded."
    LaunchRequest : Bool COMMENT "A cycle launch is possible: live CycleRequest, idle, ram at home. Fires the 0-to-10 transition once the pre-motion warning has sounded; the same fired condition resets PressureTripCount (per-cycle jam counting, REQ-048)."
    CycleAbort : Bool COMMENT "Named once (C-601): abort an in-flight cycle to Retract - Off commanded mid-cycle, or the plant acquired a stop reason (CycleInhibit). Read by the Step 10 and Step 20 exits; the Step 30 retract completes regardless, so an aborted cycle always ends parked. Jog is untouched by this bit (owner amendment 2026-07-16)."
    EndTravelTimeoutMS : DInt
    ParkedTimeoutMS : DInt
    EndTravelHoldTimeMS : DInt
    PumpRunOnTimeMS : DInt
    JogWarningTimeMS : DInt
    PressureTripConfirmTimeMS : DInt
    PressureClearResumeDelayMS : DInt
    PressureConfirmTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
    PressureClearTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
    PressureHold : Bool COMMENT "Latched jam hold, not a fault (C-123) - see the Pressure Detection network. Freezes ExtendDemand while set; clears itself once pressure has genuinely stayed clear for PressureClearResumeDelay."
    PressureConfirmEdge : Bool
    PressureConfirmEdgeMem : Bool
    PressureTripCount : Int COMMENT "Confirmed jams this cycle - reset each cycle start, not time-windowed. Compared against IO.PressureTripCountThreshold to raise Blocked."
    EndTravelTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
    HoldTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
    ParkedTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
    JogPreStartTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
    ExtendDemand : Bool
    RetractDemand : Bool
    PumpDemand : Bool COMMENT "ExtendDemand OR RetractDemand - the pump's own immediate (non-run-on) demand signal."
    PumpEverDemanded : Bool COMMENT "Cold-start guard for the pump run-on off-delay below - see that network's own comment."
    PumpRunOnTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
  TEMP
    Time : Real
  CONSTANT

NETWORK 1 "Enable And Motion Requests"
  COMMENT "The compound conditions every later network shares, each written once (C-601). Requests read Step as it settled last scan (the transitions run later) - safe, because Step only ever leaves 0 through this scan's own request-gated transitions; steps returning to 0 just re-arm the requests one scan late. CycleInhibit kills cycle requests (no launch into a stopped plant) and, via CycleAbort, retracts an in-flight cycle - while JogDemand deliberately ignores it: hand-jog stays available with the plant stopped by downstream absence (owner amendment 2026-07-16, REQ-040)."
  COIL IO.Enable := IO.Fitted AND IO.Mode <> 0
  COIL CycleRequest := (IO.Mode = 1 AND IO.HopperHighLevel OR IO.Mode = 2 AND IO.ManualCycleCmd) AND IO.Enable AND NOT IO.Blocked AND NOT IO.CycleInhibit
  COIL JogDemand := (IO.JogExtendCmd OR IO.JogRetractCmd) AND IO.Step = 0 AND IO.Mode = 2 AND IO.Fitted
  COIL ReparkRequest := (IO.Fitted AND IO.ParkCmd OR CycleRequest) AND IO.Step = 0 AND NOT IO.HomeLimit AND NOT JogDemand
  COIL LaunchRequest := CycleRequest AND IO.Step = 0 AND IO.HomeLimit
  COIL CycleAbort := IO.Mode = 0 OR IO.CycleInhibit

NETWORK 2 "Both Limit Switches Active Simultaneously"
  COMMENT "Fitted gates both the set and the hold of the latch (REQ-043/044, gate at the source): a disabled pusher raises no fault, and a fault latched while fitted clears the moment the pusher is disabled. FC_AlarmsMain reads only these already-gated bits."
  COIL IO.BothSwitchesFault := (IO.HomeLimit AND IO.FullTravelLimit OR IO.BothSwitchesFault AND NOT IO.FaultReset) AND IO.Fitted

NETWORK 3 "HMI Time Conversions"
  COMMENT "HMI/DB_Settings times are Real seconds for operator legibility; every TON below needs its PT in DInt ms - one MUL+CONVERT pair per timer, matching the MotorDOL FTTime/EnableUPSTime idiom. Kept as one block up front rather than repeated at each timer, so the x1000 idiom is visibly consistent and only ever done once."
  MUL(EN := TRUE, IN1 := IO.PressureTripConfirmTime, IN2 := 1000.0) => Time
  MUL(EN := TRUE, IN1 := IO.PressureClearResumeDelay, IN2 := 1000.0) => Time
  MUL(EN := TRUE, IN1 := IO.EndTravelTimeout, IN2 := 1000.0) => Time
  MUL(EN := TRUE, IN1 := IO.EndTravelHoldTime, IN2 := 1000.0) => Time
  MUL(EN := TRUE, IN1 := IO.ParkedTimeout, IN2 := 1000.0) => Time
  MUL(EN := TRUE, IN1 := IO.JogWarningTime, IN2 := 1000.0) => Time
  MUL(EN := TRUE, IN1 := IO.PumpRunOnTime, IN2 := 1000.0) => Time
  CONVERT(EN := ENO, IN := Time) => PressureTripConfirmTimeMS
  CONVERT(EN := ENO, IN := Time) => PressureClearResumeDelayMS
  CONVERT(EN := ENO, IN := Time) => EndTravelTimeoutMS
  CONVERT(EN := ENO, IN := Time) => EndTravelHoldTimeMS
  CONVERT(EN := ENO, IN := Time) => ParkedTimeoutMS
  CONVERT(EN := ENO, IN := Time) => JogWarningTimeMS
  CONVERT(EN := ENO, IN := Time) => PumpRunOnTimeMS

NETWORK 4 "Pre-Motion Warning"
  COMMENT "NEW-4 owner ruling (2026-07-16): no unwarned pusher motion. Every motion start from rest - repark, auto/manual cycle launch, jog - arms this timer and the sounder; the Step 0 transitions and the jog demands only act on its Q, so the sounder always leads motion by JogWarningTime. Jog keeps sounding while moving (REQ-041) because JogDemand stays true through the jog; in-cycle strokes (10/20/30, including a stop-forced retract) are continuations of an already-warned launch, so the warning boundary is Step 0. A request released mid-warning (short manual tap, hopper clearing) simply never moves. Timer and sounder keep their original jog-era names to avoid interface churn - rename queued with the cosmetic pass."
  TON(JogPreStartTimer, IN := ReparkRequest OR LaunchRequest OR JogDemand, PT := JogWarningTimeMS)
  COIL IO.JogPreStartSounder := ReparkRequest OR LaunchRequest OR JogDemand

NETWORK 5 "Pressure Trip Detection, Hold, And Counting"
  COMMENT "One function, one network: a trip must be debounced (PressureConfirmTimer) before it counts - momentary pressure spikes aren't a real jam. Hold latches through a confirmed trip and only releases once pressure has genuinely cleared for PressureClearResumeDelay, so a bouncing switch can't re-trigger the count on every scan. Count resets each cycle start (the same LaunchRequest-and-warning-done condition that fires the 0-to-10 launch), not on a rolling time window."
  TON(PressureConfirmTimer, IN := IO.Step = 10 AND IO.HighPressure, PT := PressureTripConfirmTimeMS)
  TON(PressureClearTimer, IN := PressureHold AND NOT IO.HighPressure, PT := PressureClearResumeDelayMS)
  COIL PressureHold := PressureConfirmTimer.Q OR PressureHold AND NOT PressureClearTimer.Q
  COIL PressureConfirmEdge := PressureConfirmTimer.Q AND NOT PressureConfirmEdgeMem
  COIL PressureConfirmEdgeMem := PressureConfirmTimer.Q
  MOVE(EN := LaunchRequest AND JogPreStartTimer.Q OR IO.FaultReset, IN := 0) => PressureTripCount
  ADD(EN := PressureConfirmEdge, IN1 := 1, IN2 := PressureTripCount) => PressureTripCount

NETWORK 6 "Blocked Fault (Too Many Jams)"
  COMMENT "Fitted gates set and hold (REQ-043/044, gate at the source) - a disabled pusher raises nothing, and disabling clears a standing latch."
  COIL IO.Blocked := (PressureTripCount >= IO.PressureTripCountThreshold OR IO.Blocked AND NOT IO.FaultReset) AND IO.Fitted

NETWORK 7 "Step 0 (Idle) - Warned Repark And Launch"
  COMMENT "Repark (0 to 30) fires only on a live occasion - the plant pre-start ParkCmd (REQ-045) or a cycle request arriving with the ram off home - and only after the pre-motion warning has sounded. Jog release deliberately triggers nothing: the ram stops and stays where it is (REQ-039, owner ruling 2026-07-16), and Off mode alone no longer self-parks an idle ram either - it parks at the next pre-start or cycle request. Launch (0 to 10) still requires the ram at home; a request with the ram off home reparks first, then launches if the request is still live at home. The two exits are mutually exclusive by construction (NOT HomeLimit vs HomeLimit, C-121)."
  MOVE(EN := ReparkRequest AND JogPreStartTimer.Q, IN := 30) => IO.Step
  MOVE(EN := LaunchRequest AND JogPreStartTimer.Q, IN := 10) => IO.Step

NETWORK 8 "Step 10 (Drive To End Travel) - Timer, Timeout Fault, And Transitions"
  COMMENT "Every abnormal exit - CycleAbort (Off commanded mid-stroke, or the plant acquired a stop reason), or a timeout, whether or not it also trips Blocked - goes straight to Retract (30), never a bare stop; the ram is never left sitting mid-travel. Only reaching FullTravelLimit cleanly goes to Hold (20) first, per the normal cycle. Fitted gates the supervision timer (a disabled pusher looks for no switch feedback, REQ-043) and the fault latch (raises nothing, REQ-044)."
  TON(EndTravelTimer, IN := IO.Fitted AND IO.Step = 10, PT := EndTravelTimeoutMS)
  COIL IO.EndTravelTimeoutFault := (EndTravelTimer.Q OR IO.EndTravelTimeoutFault AND NOT IO.FaultReset) AND IO.Fitted
  MOVE(EN := IO.Step = 10 AND CycleAbort, IN := 30) => IO.Step
  MOVE(EN := IO.Step = 10 AND NOT CycleAbort AND EndTravelTimer.Q, IN := 30) => IO.Step
  MOVE(EN := IO.Step = 10 AND NOT CycleAbort AND NOT EndTravelTimer.Q AND IO.Blocked, IN := 30) => IO.Step
  MOVE(EN := IO.Step = 10 AND NOT CycleAbort AND NOT EndTravelTimer.Q AND NOT IO.Blocked AND IO.FullTravelLimit, IN := 20) => IO.Step

NETWORK 9 "Step 20 (Hold) - Timer And Transition"
  TON(HoldTimer, IN := IO.Step = 20, PT := EndTravelHoldTimeMS)
  MOVE(EN := (HoldTimer.Q OR CycleAbort) AND IO.Step = 20, IN := 30) => IO.Step

NETWORK 10 "Step 30 (Retract) - Timer, Timeout Fault, And Transitions"
  COMMENT "ParkedTimer's own Q feeds the fault latch; genuinely stuck retracting has no safer intermediate step to abort into (unlike Step 10), so the recovery transition is FaultReset AND ParkedTimeoutFault straight to Step 0 (idle) - C-123's universal FaultReset-recovery rule: a fault is never left with no transition, even when 'back to idle' is the only option. Fitted gates the supervision timer and the fault latch (REQ-043/044) - a disabled pusher neither watches for the home switch nor raises the fault."
  TON(ParkedTimer, IN := IO.Fitted AND IO.Step = 30, PT := ParkedTimeoutMS)
  COIL IO.ParkedTimeoutFault := (ParkedTimer.Q OR IO.ParkedTimeoutFault AND NOT IO.FaultReset) AND IO.Fitted
  MOVE(EN := IO.Step = 30 AND IO.HomeLimit, IN := 0) => IO.Step
  MOVE(EN := IO.Step = 30 AND IO.ParkedTimeoutFault AND IO.FaultReset, IN := 0) => IO.Step

NETWORK 11 "Extend And Retract Demand"
  COMMENT "PressureHold gates ExtendDemand so a confirmed jam holds the ram in place rather than continuing to push (a hold per C-123, not a fault - it clears and driving resumes the instant pressure has cleared). Jog demand arms only after the pre-motion warning (JogPreStartTimer.Q via NETWORK 4) and re-checks Step = 0 fresh: JogDemand was computed before this scan's transitions, so a same-scan launch or repark must still kill the jog demand rather than drive both solenoids for a scan. Every term is Fitted-gated (REQ-043: a disabled pusher never demands motion) - the cycle terms explicitly, the jog terms through JogDemand's own gate."
  COIL ExtendDemand := IO.Fitted AND IO.Step = 10 AND NOT PressureHold OR JogDemand AND IO.JogExtendCmd AND JogPreStartTimer.Q AND IO.Step = 0
  COIL RetractDemand := IO.Fitted AND IO.Step = 30 OR JogDemand AND IO.JogRetractCmd AND JogPreStartTimer.Q AND IO.Step = 0

NETWORK 12 "Pump Demand"
  COIL PumpDemand := ExtendDemand OR RetractDemand
  COIL PumpEverDemanded := PumpDemand OR PumpEverDemanded

NETWORK 13 "Pump Run-On Timer And Output Commands"
  COMMENT "Off-delay built from TON+inversion, not TOF/TONR (C-406). PumpEverDemanded guards a cold-start gap: on power-up PumpDemand and the timer's Q are both initially false, which would read as 'run-on already elapsed' and skip straight to no-run. RunPowerPack stays on through the run-on tail even after demand drops, but the Extend/Retract solenoids are not - they only ever follow live demand, gated by PowerPackRunningFB so the ram can't be commanded before the pump has confirmed running. Fitted gates RunPowerPack directly too: disabling the pusher must kill the pack immediately, run-on tail included (REQ-043)."
  TON(PumpRunOnTimer, IN := NOT PumpDemand, PT := PumpRunOnTimeMS)
  COIL IO.RunPowerPack := (PumpDemand OR PumpEverDemanded AND NOT PumpRunOnTimer.Q) AND IO.Fitted
  COIL IO.Extend := ExtendDemand AND IO.PowerPackRunningFB
  COIL IO.Retract := RetractDemand AND IO.PowerPackRunningFB
  COIL IO.Cycling := IO.Step <> 0

SIDECAR
